# Apps deployed as previews right now — one app folder name per line.
#
# This file IS the deploy trigger. Every app's ignoreCommand reads it: a name
# listed here means Vercel builds a preview of that app on every push to the
# branch carrying this file. A name absent means Vercel skips, which is the
# default, and which is what `main` always looks like.
#
# It exists switched off rather than not existing, so the mechanism is visible
# to an agent reading the repo rather than discoverable only from a rule.
#
# Writing a name here is deliberate, recorded and reversible — which is what
# the On track stage needed and an empty commit could never be. The commit that
# adds a name changes what the repo does; it is not activity for its own sake.
#
# Rules:
#   - One folder name per line, exactly as it appears under apps/.
#   - Lines starting with # are comments. `# home` does NOT switch home on.
#   - An empty list is the normal state and the only state `main` may have.
#   - `drift` FAILS on main if any app is listed, so this cannot merge switched
#     on. The technical director empties it at the gate, before merging.
#
# The preview URL is derived from the branch, not invented:
#   https://<project>-git-<branch-with-slashes-and-dots-as-dashes>-tech-paddock.vercel.app
# Vercel truncates and hashes long ones, so the URL goes on the board only
# after it has been read back from a live deployment.
#
# Every *.vercel.app host is behind Vercel Authentication — measured, not
# assumed: ssoProtection is enabled for all_except_custom_domains. A preview is
# reachable by the Vercel account and nobody else, and the app's own password
# gate sits behind that.

home
